                        "sense_id": "8857971b-746f-34e3-82e0-6dce2806af9e",
                        "entry_id": "364c43a1-5c2d-3e6e-a252-8dec2165123f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A blond person whose very pale, almost white hair resembles tow; the hair of such a person."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca32e9c5-80b8-4b50-9915-c11b14c77e17",
                                "sense_id": "8857971b-746f-34e3-82e0-6dce2806af9e",
                                "text": "You've got a swell chance to make this [baseball] team, you have, not! Third base is my job, Freshie. Why, you tow-head, you couldn't play marbles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d3c4d47-92c2-40b0-8f9a-e5c4deae530e",
                                "sense_id": "8857971b-746f-34e3-82e0-6dce2806af9e",
                                "text": "Then he noticed that the scar ran back into her hair, and Lower Appalachian towhead is the nearest thing in nature you will get to platinum blond, barring albinos."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9dc8d54f-4d00-414f-acd0-5a4f8013a395",
                                "sense_id": "8857971b-746f-34e3-82e0-6dce2806af9e",
                                "text": "2010, Joseph A. West, Richard Compton (byline), Death of a Hangman, New American Library (Signet), page 103,\n“Hell, I never did cotton to an uppity whore anyhow,\" the towhead said."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1374672c-514c-4cfb-8489-f0f2af95b608",
                                "sense_id": "8857971b-746f-34e3-82e0-6dce2806af9e",
                                "text": "2012, Ann M. Paulson, Stepping Stones for the Heart, Hay House (Balboa Press), page 88,\nThe courtyard was lit with bright sunlight and Asenath and the two towheads were there amusing themselves."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a5c44820-6a9c-3a0a-8187-f0b1720a935e",
                        "entry_id": "364c43a1-5c2d-3e6e-a252-8dec2165123f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An alluvial deposit in a river, such as a sandbar, or a small island formed from silt, often permanent enough to have vegetation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d65c662f-ba80-477a-a6d8-30d7d07c5a52",
                                "sense_id": "a5c44820-6a9c-3a0a-8187-f0b1720a935e",
                                "text": "Well, the second night a fog begun to come on, and we made for a towhead to tie to, for it wouldn't do to try to run in a fog; but when I paddled ahead in the canoe, with the line to make fast, there warn't anything but little saplings to tie to."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
